    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-11941" textLabel="MONOMER-11941" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q5W7P1" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1600.0" centerY="507.6439208984375" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The rice gene &lt;i&gt;GME&lt;/i&gt; encodes a polypeptide containing NAD-binding motifs of genes from the epimerase/dehydratase family: GxxGxxG and YxxxK |CITS:[16413588]|. The gene was expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; and demonstrated to encode for a protein with GDP-D-mannose 3&quot;,5&quot;-epimerase activity |CITS:[16413588]|. The purified protein catalyzes the conversion of GDP-D-mannose into two distinct products: GDP-L-gulose and GDP-L-galactose. The equilibrium ratios of GDP-D-mannose, GDP-L-galactose and GDP-L-gulose are approximately 75%, 25% and 5%, respectively. This enzyme is assumed to be involved in ascorbate biosynthesis although genetic evidence remains to be obtained to confirm the assertion |CITS:[16413588]|. The maximum activity of the enzyme was observed at pH 7.5-8.0 in the absence of NAD&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt;. The optimal pH shifted to 8.0-8.5 when NAD&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt; was present |CITS:[16413588]|. Similarly, the optimal temperature shifted from 20ºC to 25ºC in the absence and presence of NAD&lt;sup&gt;+&lt;/sup&gt;, respectively.</Comment>
